<title>GERMANY: Kohl sees EMU on time, with Germany -Hintze.</title>
<headline>Kohl sees EMU on time, with Germany -Hintze.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor Helmut Kohl on Monday told a meeting of leaders of his Christian Democratic Union (CDU) he believes European monetary union will start on time, in accordance with the convergence criteria, and with Germany's participation, CDU general secretary Peter Hintze said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Euro will come, it will come with Germany, it will come at the time foreseen in the (Maastricht) treaty, under strict observance of the criteria,&quot; Hintze quoted Kohl as saying.</p>
<p>The start of EMU is scheduled for January 1, 1999.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
